# Local agent config, benchmarks and one-off tooling. These are personal working
# directories, not shipped source, EXCEPT the CI size/startup gates below: no
# package build or npm script reads them, so a fresh clone is unaffected by
# their absence.
/.gg/
/.claude/
# bench/ stays personal except the committed CI gates and their baseline.
/bench/*
!/bench/size-gate.mjs
!/bench/startup-gate.mjs
!/bench/baseline/
/bench/baseline/*
!/bench/baseline/sizes.json
/benchmarks/
/experiments/bench-mark/
/experiments/lean-code-bench/
/scripts/
CLAUDE.md
packages/*/.bench-*.mjs

# Local research/strategy notes
/*-vs-*.md
/*-report.md
/fixes.md
/*coding-agent*.md

# Challenge feature: design sandbox and dev-only preview harness.
#
# Neither ships. `mockups/` is the standalone HTML/CSS/JS sandbox the fight's
# visual language was designed in; `dev/` is a browser harness that mounts the
# real ActivityBar so the offer can be eyeballed without the Tauri runtime.
# Vite builds a single entry (index.html), so a production build never sees
# them — a clean build emits dist/index.html and nothing else. Ignored so
# `git add -A` cannot sweep 216KB of scratch into a release.
/gg-app/mockups/
/gg-app/dev/
